    2                      ;  03_set_compare -- all 22 set-compares, signed against unsigned
    3                      ;=============================================================================
    4                      ;  Checklist: A7 (R-type signed), A8 (R-type unsigned), A9 (I-type signed),
    5                      ;             A10 (I-type unsigned).
    6                      ;
    7                      ;  These are the instructions this CPU got wrong twice: the four R-type
    8                      ;  unsigned compares were missing from CU_HW_LUT's func case and trapped as
    9                      ;  illegal, and the four I-type unsigned ones decoded to the SIGNED ALU op, so
   10                      ;  every result was inverted.  Both bugs are invisible unless a test compares
   11                      ;  a value whose sign bit is set against a small positive one -- which is what
   12                      ;  every block below does.
   13                      ;
   14                      ;  Blocks, in order:
   15                      ;    words  0..9   R-type, -1 vs 1       (signed: less; unsigned: greater)
   16                      ;    words 10..19  R-type, 1 vs 1        (the equality boundary)
   17                      ;    words 20..23  R-type, INT_MIN vs INT_MAX  (signed and unsigned disagree)
   18                      ;    words 24..33  I-type, -1 vs 1
   19                      ;    words 34..43  I-type, 1 vs 1
   20                      ;    words 44..47  I-type, the immediate's own extension
   21                      ;
   22                      ;  Within a block the order is always:
   23                      ;    seq sne slt sgt sle sge sltu sgtu sleu sgeu
   24                      ;=============================================================================
   25  00000000          	
   26  00000000          	.text
   27  00000000          	
   28  00000000  2001ffff	addi r1, r0, -1             ; 0xFFFFFFFF : -1 signed, 4294967295 unsigned
